' 4+1 scenarios (+1) - use cases
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: everyone (product, whoever writes the code, whoever evaluates).
' Documented decision: which use cases cut across the other views and validate them; each one is a scenario (SC-) of scenarios.md, which links it to the backlog stories, the process diagrams and the tests.
' Not drawn: the sequence of each scenario (the scenarios point to the process-*.puml files); P-CLI and P-OPS, who do not use the application (see c4/README.md).
@startuml scenarios-use-cases
!include ../style.puml

title Scenarios - use cases
left to right direction

actor "Visitor" as P_VIS
actor "Player" as P_JOG
actor "Owner" as P_DONO
actor "Admin" as P_ADMIN

rectangle "Pitch Booking App" {
    usecase "Searches for and books a slot" as SC_01
    usecase "Sets up club, pitches,\nschedules and prices" as SC_02
    usecase "Cancels a booking\nin the calendar" as SC_03
    usecase "Weekly booking\nwith one date skipped" as SC_04
    usecase "Recovers the password" as SC_05
    usecase "Deactivates an owner" as SC_06
    usecase "Race for the same slot" as SC_07
}

P_VIS --> SC_01
P_VIS --> SC_05
P_JOG --> SC_01
P_JOG --> SC_04
P_JOG --> SC_07
P_DONO --> SC_02
P_DONO --> SC_03
P_ADMIN --> SC_06

SC_04 ..> SC_01 : <<include>>
SC_07 ..> SC_01 : <<include>>
@enduml
